title: Coalition Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 1 and coalition_affairs_timer = 0 and (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition)
card-image: img/muller_cabinet.jpg

= Coalition Affairs

Our coalition is in trouble. Our partners in the [+ coalition_name +] complain about our policies in every talk show, and the coalition committee meets more often than the cabinet. [? if coalition_dissent >= 2 : There is open talk of ending the coalition. ?]

How do we reduce tensions in the coalition?

- @promise_cuts: Agree to our partners' plans for spending cuts.
- @resources: Use our party resources to smooth things over.
- @bring_down: End the coalition ourselves and go for new elections.
- @no_change: Take none of these actions.
- @easy_discard


@promise_cuts
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 6; workers_linke += 5; unemployed_linke += 3; unemployed_afd += 3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; welfare -= 1; budget += 1; coalition_dissent = 0

Fine. We agree to a round of cuts, and the coalition is calm again.

@resources
subtitle: -2 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2).
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1

We give way on a few posts and projects that our partners care about. It is horse-trading, but it keeps the government working.

@no_change

No. We will not do this.

@bring_down
subtitle: End this government before our partners do.
view-if: chancellor_party = "SPD"
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; coalition_dissent = 0; left_strength += 8; trust_in_democracy -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 2; old_middle_spd -= 2; reformist_dissent += 5
call: set_next_election_time

[+ chancellor +] dismisses the ministers of our partners and asks the Bundestag the confidence question, losing it on purpose. The president dissolves the Bundestag, and we carry on until the election.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
